@startuml checkout_sequence
' ============================================================================
' Village Storefront - Checkout & Payment Sequence Diagram (PlantUML)
' ============================================================================
' Description: Authoritative checkout orchestration flow documenting tenant
'              resolution, saga-pattern compensations, Stripe integration,
'              loyalty operations, and audit logging.
'
' References:
'   - ADR-003: Checkout Saga Pattern (Orchestration & Compensation)
'   - Architecture: docs/architecture/04_Operational_Architecture.md §3.2.7
'   - Mermaid Version: docs/diagrams/sequence_checkout_payment.mmd
'   - OpenAPI: /checkout/preview, /checkout/commit
'
' Render with PlantUML:
'   plantuml docs/diagrams/checkout_sequence.puml
'   or
'   java -jar plantuml.jar docs/diagrams/checkout_sequence.puml
'
' Operational Use: This diagram is the authoritative reference for ops
'   and QA teams understanding checkout failure modes and compensations.
'   See platform_ops.md §5 for related runbooks.
' ============================================================================

!define SUCCESS_COLOR #E8F5E9
!define ERROR_COLOR #FFEBEE
!define WARNING_COLOR #FFF3E0
!define INFO_COLOR #E3F2FD

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10

title Village Storefront - Checkout & Payment Orchestration Flow

actor "Shopper" as Shopper
participant "Tenant Access\nGateway" as TAG
participant "TenantContext\nResolver" as TenantContext
participant "Feature Toggle\nService" as FeatureFlags
participant "Qute Storefront\nTemplate" as Storefront
participant "Checkout\nOrchestrator" as Checkout
participant "Idempotency\nStore (DB)" as IdempotencyStore
participant "Address\nValidator" as AddressValidator
participant "Carrier Rate\nAdapter" as CarrierAdapter
participant "Rate Cache\n(Caffeine)" as RateCache
participant "Inventory\nService" as Inventory
participant "Loyalty\nService" as Loyalty
participant "Stripe\nAdapter" as StripeAdapter
participant "Stripe API" as Stripe
participant "Audit Log\nService" as AuditLog
participant "PostgreSQL" as Database
participant "Background\nJob Queue" as JobQueue

' ============================================================================
' SCENARIO 1: HAPPY PATH - CHECKOUT PREVIEW
' ============================================================================

box "SCENARIO 1: Checkout Preview (Happy Path)" SUCCESS_COLOR
    note over Shopper, JobQueue
        Customer views checkout with shipping rates
        Demonstrates tenant resolution + address validation + rate shopping
    end note
end box

Shopper -> TAG: HTTPS GET {tenant}.platform.com/checkout
activate TAG

note right of TAG
    Extract subdomain or resolve custom domain
    Enforce suspension/billing status
end note

TAG -> TenantContext: resolveTenant(domain)
activate TenantContext
TenantContext -> Database: SELECT * FROM stores\nWHERE subdomain = ? OR custom_domain = ?
activate Database
Database --> TenantContext: Store(id, tenantId, status)
deactivate Database
TenantContext --> TAG: TenantContext(tenantId, storeId)
deactivate TenantContext

note right of TAG
    TenantContext propagated via CDI RequestScoped bean
    Available to all downstream services
end note

TAG -> FeatureFlags: publishTenantResolvedEvent(TenantContext)
activate FeatureFlags
FeatureFlags --> TAG: Feature snapshot loaded
deactivate FeatureFlags

TAG -> Storefront: forward(request, TenantContext, flags)
activate Storefront

Storefront -> Checkout: POST /api/v1/checkout/preview\n(cart, shippingAddress)
activate Checkout

' SAGA STAGE 1: Address Validation
group SAGA STAGE 1: Address Validation [read-only, no compensation]
    note over Checkout, AddressValidator
        Span: CheckoutSaga.addressValidation
        Metric: checkout.address_validation_latency
    end note

    Checkout -> AddressValidator: validate(Address)
    activate AddressValidator
    AddressValidator -> AddressValidator: Normalize via USPS/Lob.com API\nTimeout: 5s, Retry: 2x

    alt Address Valid
        AddressValidator --> Checkout: ValidatedAddress\n(normalized, confidence: high)
        deactivate AddressValidator

        note right of Checkout
            Audit event: checkout.address.validated
            TenantContext: tenantId captured in event
        end note

        Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.address.validated", tenantContext)
        activate AuditLog
        AuditLog -> Database: INSERT INTO audit_log\n(tenant_id, event_type, metadata)
        activate Database
        deactivate Database
        deactivate AuditLog

    else Address Invalid/Ambiguous
        AddressValidator --> Checkout: ValidationError\n(suggestions, confidence: low)
        deactivate AddressValidator

        Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.address.invalid", tenantContext, suggestions)
        activate AuditLog
        deactivate AuditLog

        Checkout --> Storefront: HTTP 400 ProblemDetails\ntype: address-validation-failed
        deactivate Checkout
        Storefront --> Shopper: Show address corrections UI
        deactivate Storefront
        deactivate TAG

        note over Checkout
            NO COMPENSATION NEEDED
            Read-only operation, no state changed
        end note
        [o<- Shopper: Flow ends
    end
end

' SAGA STAGE 2: Shipping Rate Shopping
group SAGA STAGE 2: Shipping Rate Calculation [cached, fallback on failure]
    note over Checkout, CarrierAdapter
        Span: ShippingRateAdapter.quote
        Metric: checkout.rate_cache_hit_ratio
    end note

    Checkout -> RateCache: get(cartHash + addressHash)
    activate RateCache

    alt Cache HIT
        RateCache --> Checkout: CachedRates(rates[], TTL: 15min)
        deactivate RateCache

        note right of Checkout
            Metric: checkout.rate_cache_hit++
            No external API call needed
        end note

    else Cache MISS
        RateCache --> Checkout: null
        deactivate RateCache

        Checkout -> CarrierAdapter: getRates(address, packages)
        activate CarrierAdapter
        CarrierAdapter -> CarrierAdapter: Call UPS/FedEx/USPS APIs\nTimeout: 5s per carrier, Retry: 2x

        alt Carriers Respond Successfully
            CarrierAdapter --> Checkout: ShippingRates[]\n(carrier, service, cost, ETA)
            deactivate CarrierAdapter

            Checkout -> RateCache: put(rates, TTL: 15min)
            activate RateCache
            deactivate RateCache

            Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.rates.fetched", tenantContext, rateCount)
            activate AuditLog
            deactivate AuditLog

        else All Carriers Timeout/Unavailable
            CarrierAdapter --> Checkout: CarrierError(allFailed)
            deactivate CarrierAdapter

            note right of Checkout: FALLBACK STRATEGY ACTIVATED

            Checkout -> Database: SELECT fallback_shipping_rate\nFROM tenant_settings\nWHERE tenant_id = ?
            activate Database
            Database --> Checkout: FallbackRate($5.00 flat rate)
            deactivate Database

            Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.shipping.fallback", tenantContext)
            activate AuditLog
            deactivate AuditLog

            note right of Checkout
                Metric: checkout.shipping_api_errors++
                Alert: shipping.rate.fallback (P2)
            end note
        end
    end
end

' Calculate totals and return preview
Checkout -> Checkout: Calculate totals\n(subtotal + tax + shipping)
Checkout --> Storefront: CheckoutPreview\n(total, lineItems, rates[], warnings[])
deactivate Checkout

Storefront --> Shopper: Render review page\n(totals, shipping options, payment form)
deactivate Storefront
deactivate TAG

' ============================================================================
' SCENARIO 2: HAPPY PATH - CHECKOUT COMMIT WITH LOYALTY
' ============================================================================

box "SCENARIO 2: Checkout Commit (Happy Path with Loyalty)" SUCCESS_COLOR
    note over Shopper, JobQueue
        Customer completes payment with loyalty points redemption
        Demonstrates full saga with inventory hold + loyalty hold + payment
    end note
end box

Shopper -> TAG: POST /checkout/commit\nX-Idempotency-Key: {UUID}\n(paymentMethodId, selectedRate, loyaltyPoints: 500)
activate TAG

TAG -> TenantContext: resolveTenant(domain)
activate TenantContext
TenantContext --> TAG: TenantContext(tenantId)
deactivate TenantContext

TAG -> Storefront: forward(request, TenantContext)
activate Storefront

Storefront -> Checkout: commitCheckout(CheckoutCommitRequest)
activate Checkout

' Idempotency check
group Idempotency Guard
    note over Checkout, IdempotencyStore
        Prevents duplicate order creation on network retries
        24-hour idempotency window per RFC 7231
    end note

    Checkout -> IdempotencyStore: findByKey(idempotencyKey)
    activate IdempotencyStore

    alt Key Exists (Duplicate Request)
        IdempotencyStore --> Checkout: ExistingResult(orderId, status: SUCCESS)
        deactivate IdempotencyStore

        Checkout --> Storefront: HTTP 409 Conflict\nLocation: /orders/{orderId}
        deactivate Checkout
        Storefront --> Shopper: Redirect to existing order
        deactivate Storefront
        deactivate TAG
        [o<- Shopper: Flow ends (idempotent response)

    else Key Not Found (New Request)
        IdempotencyStore --> Checkout: null
        deactivate IdempotencyStore

        Checkout -> IdempotencyStore: store(key, status: PENDING, timestamp)
        activate IdempotencyStore
        deactivate IdempotencyStore
    end
end

' SAGA STAGE 3: Re-validate address (defensive)
group SAGA STAGE 3: Address Re-validation [defensive check]
    note over Checkout, AddressValidator: Defensive check to catch client-side manipulation

    Checkout -> AddressValidator: validate(shippingAddress)
    activate AddressValidator
    AddressValidator --> Checkout: ValidatedAddress
    deactivate AddressValidator
end

' SAGA STAGE 4: Inventory Reservation
group SAGA STAGE 4: Inventory Hold [COMPENSATION POINT: release on failure]
    note over Checkout, Inventory
        Span: CheckoutSaga.inventoryReservation
        CRITICAL: Must compensate if subsequent stages fail
    end note

    Checkout -> Inventory: reserveStock(lineItems[], tenantId)
    activate Inventory

    Inventory -> Database: BEGIN TRANSACTION\nSELECT FOR UPDATE inventory_levels\nWHERE variant_id IN (...) AND tenant_id = ?
    activate Database

    alt Stock Available
        Database --> Inventory: Rows locked (qty sufficient)
        Inventory -> Database: INSERT inventory_reservations\n(cart_id, variant_id, qty, expires_at: +15min)
        Database --> Inventory: Reservation IDs
        deactivate Database

        Inventory --> Checkout: ReservationIds[]\n(expires in 15 minutes)
        deactivate Inventory

        Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.inventory.reserved", tenantContext, reservationIds)
        activate AuditLog
        deactivate AuditLog

    else Out of Stock
        Database --> Inventory: Insufficient stock for variant XYZ
        deactivate Database
        Inventory --> Checkout: OutOfStockError(variantId, available, requested)
        deactivate Inventory

        Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.inventory.insufficient", tenantContext, variantId)
        activate AuditLog
        deactivate AuditLog

        Checkout -> IdempotencyStore: update(key, status: FAILED, error)
        activate IdempotencyStore
        deactivate IdempotencyStore

        Checkout --> Storefront: HTTP 400 ProblemDetails\ntype: out-of-stock
        deactivate Checkout
        Storefront --> Shopper: Show stock error + refresh cart
        deactivate Storefront
        deactivate TAG
        [o<- Shopper: Flow ends

        note over Checkout
            NO COMPENSATION NEEDED
            No reservations created, transaction rolled back
        end note
    end
end

' SAGA STAGE 5: Loyalty Point Hold
group SAGA STAGE 5: Loyalty Hold [COMPENSATION POINT: release on failure]
    note over Checkout, Loyalty
        Hold loyalty points during checkout
        CRITICAL: Must release if payment fails
    end note

    alt Loyalty Points Requested (500 points = $5.00)
        Checkout -> Loyalty: holdPoints(customerId, tenantId, points: 500)
        activate Loyalty

        Loyalty -> Database: BEGIN TRANSACTION\nSELECT FOR UPDATE loyalty_accounts\nWHERE customer_id = ? AND tenant_id = ?
        activate Database

        alt Sufficient Points
            Database --> Loyalty: Account balance: 1200 points
            Loyalty -> Database: INSERT loyalty_holds\n(customer_id, points, expires_at: +15min, reason: "checkout")
            Database --> Loyalty: Hold ID
            deactivate Database

            Loyalty --> Checkout: LoyaltyHold(holdId, points: 500, discount: $5.00)
            deactivate Loyalty

            Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.loyalty.held", tenantContext, holdId, points)
            activate AuditLog
            deactivate AuditLog

        else Insufficient Points
            Database --> Loyalty: Account balance: 200 points (insufficient)
            deactivate Database
            Loyalty --> Checkout: InsufficientPointsError
            deactivate Loyalty

            note over Checkout: COMPENSATION SAGA BEGINS

            Checkout -> Inventory: releaseReservations(reservationIds)
            activate Inventory
            Inventory -> Database: DELETE FROM inventory_reservations\nWHERE id IN (?)
            activate Database
            deactivate Database
            deactivate Inventory

            Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.compensation.inventory_released", tenantContext)
            activate AuditLog
            deactivate AuditLog

            Checkout -> IdempotencyStore: update(key, status: FAILED)
            activate IdempotencyStore
            deactivate IdempotencyStore

            Checkout --> Storefront: HTTP 400 ProblemDetails\ntype: insufficient-loyalty-points
            deactivate Checkout
            Storefront --> Shopper: Show loyalty error
            deactivate Storefront
            deactivate TAG
            [o<- Shopper: Flow ends
        end

    else No Loyalty Points Requested
        note over Checkout: Skip loyalty hold stage
    end
end

' SAGA STAGE 6: Order Creation (tentative)
group SAGA STAGE 6: Order Creation [COMPENSATION POINT: mark CANCELLED on payment failure]
    note over Checkout, Database
        Create order in PENDING_PAYMENT status
        Will transition to PROCESSING on payment success
    end note

    Checkout -> Database: BEGIN TRANSACTION\nINSERT INTO orders\n(tenant_id, status: PENDING_PAYMENT, total, loyalty_discount)\nINSERT INTO order_items
    activate Database
    Database --> Checkout: Order(id, orderNumber, status)
    deactivate Database

    Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("order.created", tenantContext, orderId, status: PENDING_PAYMENT)
    activate AuditLog
    deactivate AuditLog
end

' SAGA STAGE 7: Payment Processing
group SAGA STAGE 7: Payment Authorization [CRITICAL FAILURE POINT]
    note over Checkout, Stripe
        Span: StripeIntentService.commit
        Idempotency: Stripe API uses orderId as idempotency key
        CRITICAL: Requires full compensation on failure
    end note

    Checkout -> StripeAdapter: createPaymentIntent(\norder, paymentMethodId,\nidempotencyKey: orderId)
    activate StripeAdapter

    StripeAdapter -> Stripe: POST /v1/payment_intents\namount: $45.00 (total - loyalty discount)\npayment_method: pm_xxx\nidempotency_key: order_{orderId}\nmetadata: {tenantId, orderId}
    activate Stripe

    alt Payment Authorized Successfully
        Stripe --> StripeAdapter: PaymentIntent\n(status: succeeded, charge_id)
        deactivate Stripe
        StripeAdapter --> Checkout: PaymentIntent(succeeded, chargeId)
        deactivate StripeAdapter

        Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("payment.authorized", tenantContext, orderId, chargeId)
        activate AuditLog
        deactivate AuditLog

        ' Finalize order
        Checkout -> Database: BEGIN TRANSACTION\nUPDATE orders\nSET status = PROCESSING, payment_intent_id = ?, paid_at = NOW()\nUPDATE inventory_reservations SET status = COMMITTED\nDELETE FROM loyalty_holds WHERE id = ? (convert to transaction)
        activate Database
        Database --> Checkout: Commit successful
        deactivate Database

        Checkout -> Loyalty: commitHold(holdId) -- converts hold to points deduction
        activate Loyalty
        Loyalty -> Database: UPDATE loyalty_accounts\nSET balance = balance - 500\nWHERE customer_id = ? AND tenant_id = ?
        activate Database
        deactivate Database
        deactivate Loyalty

        Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("order.paid", tenantContext, orderId, paymentMethod)
        activate AuditLog
        deactivate AuditLog

        Checkout -> IdempotencyStore: update(key, status: SUCCESS, orderId)
        activate IdempotencyStore
        deactivate IdempotencyStore

        ' Enqueue background jobs
        Checkout -> JobQueue: enqueue(SendOrderConfirmationEmail, orderId)
        activate JobQueue
        deactivate JobQueue

        Checkout -> JobQueue: enqueue(CreateShippingLabel, orderId)
        activate JobQueue
        deactivate JobQueue

        Checkout -> JobQueue: enqueue(AwardLoyaltyPoints, customerId, points: 45)
        activate JobQueue
        deactivate JobQueue

        Checkout --> Storefront: OrderCreatedResponse\n(orderId, orderNumber, total)
        deactivate Checkout

        Storefront --> Shopper: HTTP 201 Created\nLocation: /orders/{orderId}\nRedirect to confirmation page
        deactivate Storefront
        deactivate TAG

    else Payment Declined
        Stripe --> StripeAdapter: PaymentError\n(decline_code: insufficient_funds, message)
        deactivate Stripe
        StripeAdapter --> Checkout: PaymentError(decline_code, message)
        deactivate StripeAdapter

        note over Checkout: *** COMPENSATION SAGA BEGINS ***

        box "COMPENSATION FLOW" ERROR_COLOR
            note over Checkout, Database
                Roll back all saga stages in reverse order
                Ensure no partial state remains
            end note
        end box

        ' Compensation 1: Release loyalty hold
        alt Loyalty Hold Exists
            Checkout -> Loyalty: releaseHold(holdId)
            activate Loyalty
            Loyalty -> Database: DELETE FROM loyalty_holds WHERE id = ?
            activate Database
            deactivate Database
            deactivate Loyalty

            Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.compensation.loyalty_released", tenantContext, holdId)
            activate AuditLog
            deactivate AuditLog
        end

        ' Compensation 2: Release inventory reservations
        Checkout -> Inventory: releaseReservations(reservationIds)
        activate Inventory
        Inventory -> Database: DELETE FROM inventory_reservations WHERE id IN (?)
        activate Database
        deactivate Database
        deactivate Inventory

        Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.compensation.inventory_released", tenantContext, reservationIds)
        activate AuditLog
        deactivate AuditLog

        ' Compensation 3: Cancel order
        Checkout -> Database: UPDATE orders\nSET status = CANCELLED, cancellation_reason = 'payment_failed'\nWHERE id = ?
        activate Database
        deactivate Database

        Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("order.cancelled", tenantContext, orderId, reason: payment_failed)
        activate AuditLog
        deactivate AuditLog

        ' Update idempotency key
        Checkout -> IdempotencyStore: update(key, status: FAILED, error: decline_code)
        activate IdempotencyStore
        deactivate IdempotencyStore

        note over Checkout
            Metric: checkout.payment.declined++
            Alert: None (customer-side error, expected)
        end note

        Checkout --> Storefront: HTTP 402 Payment Required\ntype: payment-declined\ndetail: {decline_code, message}
        deactivate Checkout

        Storefront --> Shopper: Show payment error\n(retry with different method)
        deactivate Storefront
        deactivate TAG
    end
end

' ============================================================================
' SCENARIO 3: CARRIER API FAILURE WITH FALLBACK
' ============================================================================

box "SCENARIO 3: Carrier API Failure (Fallback Strategy)" WARNING_COLOR
    note over Shopper, JobQueue
        All shipping carriers unavailable during preview
        System falls back to tenant-configured flat rate
    end note
end box

Shopper -> TAG: POST /checkout/preview
activate TAG
TAG -> TenantContext: resolveTenant(domain)
activate TenantContext
TenantContext --> TAG: TenantContext
deactivate TenantContext
TAG -> Storefront: forward(request, TenantContext)
activate Storefront
Storefront -> Checkout: previewCheckout(cart, address)
activate Checkout

group Address Validation (succeeds)
    Checkout -> AddressValidator: validate(address)
    activate AddressValidator
    AddressValidator --> Checkout: ValidatedAddress
    deactivate AddressValidator
end

group Shipping Rate Fetch (all carriers fail)
    Checkout -> CarrierAdapter: getRates(address, packages)
    activate CarrierAdapter

    CarrierAdapter -> CarrierAdapter: UPS API: Timeout (5s)\nFedEx API: HTTP 503\nUSPS API: Network error

    CarrierAdapter --> Checkout: AllCarriersFailedError
    deactivate CarrierAdapter

    note right of Checkout: FALLBACK STRATEGY

    Checkout -> Database: SELECT fallback_shipping_rate\nFROM tenant_settings WHERE tenant_id = ?
    activate Database
    Database --> Checkout: FallbackRate($5.00, name: "Standard Shipping (estimated)")
    deactivate Database

    Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("checkout.shipping.fallback_used", tenantContext)
    activate AuditLog
    deactivate AuditLog

    note right of Checkout
        Metric: checkout.shipping.fallback++
        Alert: shipping.rate.fallback (P2 warning)
        Ops Action: Check carrier status pages
    end note

    Checkout -> Checkout: Build preview with fallback rate + warning flag
end

Checkout --> Storefront: CheckoutPreview\n(total with $5.00 shipping,\nwarning: "Shipping estimate, actual cost calculated at fulfillment")
deactivate Checkout

Storefront --> Shopper: Show totals + warning banner:\n"Shipping carriers temporarily unavailable, estimated rate shown"
deactivate Storefront
deactivate TAG

' ============================================================================
' SCENARIO 4: WEBHOOK RECONCILIATION (PAYMENT SUCCESS BUT NETWORK TIMEOUT)
' ============================================================================

box "SCENARIO 4: Payment Success + Network Failure (Webhook Reconciliation)" INFO_COLOR
    note over Shopper, JobQueue
        Payment succeeds at Stripe but HTTP response lost
        Client retries with same idempotency key
        Stripe's idempotency ensures no double-charge
    end note
end box

Shopper -> TAG: POST /checkout/commit\nX-Idempotency-Key: abc-123 (first attempt)
activate TAG
TAG -> Storefront: forward(request, TenantContext)
activate Storefront
Storefront -> Checkout: commitCheckout(request)
activate Checkout

note over Checkout: Idempotency key stored, saga executes...\nInventory reserved, order created, payment initiated...

Checkout -> StripeAdapter: createPaymentIntent(order, paymentMethod,\nidempotencyKey: order_789)
activate StripeAdapter
StripeAdapter -> Stripe: POST /v1/payment_intents\n(idempotency_key: order_789)
activate Stripe

note over Stripe: Payment succeeds, charge created\n$45.00 captured from customer card

Stripe --x StripeAdapter: Network timeout\n(HTTP response lost)
deactivate Stripe

note over StripeAdapter: TCP connection broken before response read

StripeAdapter --x Checkout: NetworkException (timeout)
deactivate StripeAdapter

note over Checkout: Exception propagates up\nOrder remains in PENDING_PAYMENT status\nIdempotency key status: PENDING

Checkout --x Storefront: HTTP 500 (timeout)
deactivate Checkout
Storefront --x Shopper: Error: "Unable to process payment"
deactivate Storefront
deactivate TAG

note over Shopper
    Client retries checkout with SAME idempotency key
    Stripe will return existing PaymentIntent (idempotent)
end note

Shopper -> TAG: POST /checkout/commit\nX-Idempotency-Key: abc-123 (retry with same key)
activate TAG
TAG -> Storefront: forward(request, TenantContext)
activate Storefront
Storefront -> Checkout: commitCheckout(request)
activate Checkout

Checkout -> IdempotencyStore: findByKey(abc-123)
activate IdempotencyStore
IdempotencyStore --> Checkout: Entry(status: PENDING, orderId: 789)
deactivate IdempotencyStore

note over Checkout
    Idempotency key exists but status still PENDING
    Re-attempt checkout saga from payment stage
end note

Checkout -> StripeAdapter: createPaymentIntent(order_789, ...,\nidempotencyKey: order_789)
activate StripeAdapter
StripeAdapter -> Stripe: POST /v1/payment_intents\n(idempotency_key: order_789)
activate Stripe

note over Stripe
    Stripe recognizes idempotency key
    Returns EXISTING PaymentIntent (no new charge)
end note

Stripe --> StripeAdapter: PaymentIntent\n(status: succeeded, charge_id: ch_xyz)\n[Idempotent response]
deactivate Stripe
StripeAdapter --> Checkout: PaymentIntent(succeeded)
deactivate StripeAdapter

note over Checkout
    Detect payment already succeeded
    Finalize order normally (idempotent operations)
end note

Checkout -> Database: UPDATE orders SET status = PROCESSING\nWHERE id = 789 AND status = PENDING_PAYMENT
activate Database
Database --> Checkout: 1 row updated
deactivate Database

Checkout -> IdempotencyStore: update(key: abc-123, status: SUCCESS, orderId: 789)
activate IdempotencyStore
deactivate IdempotencyStore

Checkout -> AuditLog: logEvent("order.reconciled_from_webhook", tenantContext, orderId)
activate AuditLog
deactivate AuditLog

Checkout --> Storefront: OrderCreatedResponse(orderId: 789)
deactivate Checkout
Storefront --> Shopper: HTTP 201 Created\nLocation: /orders/789
deactivate Storefront
deactivate TAG

note over Shopper, Stripe
    Alternative reconciliation path:
    Stripe webhook "payment_intent.succeeded" received asynchronously
    Webhook handler queries orders table for PENDING_PAYMENT + matching payment_intent_id
    Transitions order to PROCESSING if found (same result)
end note

' ============================================================================
' LEGEND & NOTES
' ============================================================================

legend right
    **Saga Stages & Compensation Summary**

    | Stage | Operation | Compensation on Failure |
    |-------|-----------|------------------------|
    | 1. Address Validation | Normalize address (USPS) | None (read-only) |
    | 2. Shipping Rate Fetch | Query carriers (UPS/FedEx) | Fallback to flat rate |
    | 3. Address Re-validation | Defensive check | None (read-only) |
    | 4. Inventory Hold | Reserve stock (15min TTL) | DELETE reservations |
    | 5. Loyalty Hold | Hold points (15min TTL) | DELETE holds |
    | 6. Order Creation | INSERT order (PENDING_PAYMENT) | UPDATE status = CANCELLED |
    | 7. Payment Processing | Stripe PaymentIntent | Release inventory + loyalty + cancel order |

    **Observability**
    - Spans: CheckoutSaga.{addressValidation, inventoryReservation, payment}
    - Metrics: checkout.{rate_cache_hit_ratio, shipping_api_errors, payment.declined}
    - Audit Events: All saga stages + compensations logged with TenantContext

    **Idempotency**
    - Client-provided X-Idempotency-Key (UUID, 24-hour window)
    - Stripe API: orderId used as idempotency key (prevents double-charge)
    - Network retry safety: Same key returns existing result

    **Operational Runbooks**
    - Shipping fallback: See platform_ops.md §5 "Carrier API Failure"
    - Payment decline: Expected behavior, no ops action (customer retry)
    - Webhook reconciliation: Automatic, orphaned orders reconciled within 5 minutes

    **References**
    - ADR-003: Checkout Saga Pattern & Compensation
    - Architecture: docs/architecture/04_Operational_Architecture.md §3.2.7-3.2.8
    - Mermaid Version: docs/diagrams/sequence_checkout_payment.mmd (design artifact)
    - Platform Ops: docs/architecture/platform_ops.md §5-7
end legend

@enduml
